From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: Define USERPROFILE before the user's environment

Multi-user debt D15. Windows defines the user's profile variables before it
reads HKCU\Environment, so a user's variables can name the profile:
TEMP=%USERPROFILE%\AppData\Local\Temp, as REG_EXPAND_SZ. Wine read
HKCU\Environment first and set USERPROFILE only from Volatile Environment,
afterwards, which wineboot writes -- so such a TEMP stayed unexpanded, and
programs saw a TEMP of "C:\%USERPROFILE%\AppData\Local\Temp".

That order mattered little while every Wine user had a hive of their own with
absolute paths. With one Default User template seeding every user of a shared
prefix, the template must not carry anyone's absolute path, so it names the
profile instead -- and USERPROFILE must be defined first: ProfilesDirectory
(HKLM ProfileList) plus the user's name. Volatile Environment, when present,
sets the same value again.

Tested: as a second Unix user of a shared prefix, with HKCU\Environment's TEMP
and TMP set to %USERPROFILE%\AppData\Local\Temp and no Volatile Environment,
a new process sees TEMP=C:\users\sgconf\AppData\Local\Temp and
USERPROFILE=C:\users\sgconf.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -1295,6 +1295,36 @@
         add_registry_variables( env, pos, size, key );
         NtClose( key );
     }
+    /* Stained Glass OS (multi-user debt D15): the user's profile directory
+     * is defined before the user's own variables, as Windows does, so they
+     * can name it -- TEMP=%USERPROFILE%\AppData\Local\Temp. A Default User
+     * template shared by every user of a prefix then need not carry anyone's
+     * absolute path. Volatile Environment, when present, sets it again below,
+     * to the same value. */
+    init_unicode_string( &nameW, profileW );
+    if (user_name && !NtOpenKey( &key, KEY_READ, &attr ))
+    {
+        static const WCHAR profdirW[] = {'P','r','o','f','i','l','e','s','D','i','r','e','c','t','o','r','y',0};
+        static const WCHAR userprofW[] = {'U','S','E','R','P','R','O','F','I','L','E',0};
+        WCHAR *path;
+        size_t len, ulen = strlen( user_name );
+
+        if ((value = get_registry_value( *env, *pos, key, profdirW )))
+        {
+            len = wcslen( value );
+            if (len && (path = malloc( (len + ulen + 2) * sizeof(WCHAR) )))
+            {
+                memcpy( path, value, len * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+                path[len] = '\\';
+                path[len + 1 + ntdll_umbstowcs( user_name, ulen, path + len + 1, ulen )] = 0;
+                set_env_var( env, pos, size, userprofW, wcslen(userprofW), path );
+                free( path );
+            }
+            free( value );
+        }
+        NtClose( key );
+    }
+
     if (!open_hkcu_key( "Environment", &key ))
     {
         add_registry_variables( env, pos, size, key );
